  "oracle_attribution": "The new protected test test-uiplib.c directly calls the uip_nat64addr macro (test_nat64_macro) and exercises the new mixed IPv4 dotted-decimal notation added to uiplib_ip6addrconv and the new ip64_addr_is_ip64 branch in uiplib_ipaddr_snprint. uip_nat64addr is absent at base (verified: base os/net/ipv6/ip64-addr.h contains only the ip64_addr_is_ipv4_mapped_addr macro) and is added by this PR, so the before state is source-blocked. The missing interface is the PR's purpose (NAT64 / RFC 4291 mixed notation support), not an incidental helper, so a semantic compile oracle applies.",
